The meta.json file allows you to set authors, title, ratings, warnings, links, and credits.

If you add "author": "your_name", it will display in the author section./NOBR
If you instead write "authors" it will display 'Authors: {meta_authors}' instead of 'Author: {meta_author}'.

Add "rating": "your_rating" to set a rating./NOBR
Ratings are 0-3./NOBR
0 = General Audiences, 1 = Teen, 2 = Explicit, 3 = Adult

Add "links": "your_links" to set links to your pages.

Add "warnings": "your_warnings" to set warnings.

Add "credits": "your_credits" to set credits.

Add "title": "your_title" to set the title.

A fully-filled-out meta.json would look like this:/CLRB
{/NOBR/CONT
  "author": "benheroblaw",/NOBR/CONT
  "title": "testing stuff",/NOBR/CONT
  "rating": 1,/NOBR/CONT
  "links": "https://benheroblaw.github.io",/NOBR/CONT/ESC
  "warnings": "swearing",/NOBR/CONT
  "credits": "benheroblaw for coding the whole thing"/NOBR/CONT
}/CONT

And display as this:
Title:    testing stuff/NOBR/CONT
Folder:   ./content/zzz-testing//NOBR/CONT
Rating:   Teen/NOBR/CONT
Warnings: swearing/NOBR/CONT
Author:   benheroblaw/NOBR/CONT
Links:    https://benheroblaw.github.io/ESC/NOBR/CONT
Credits:  benheroblaw for coding the whole thing/NOBR/CONT